Add map key; serve a standards-mode page on Pages

The hosted copy was the Artifact build, which has no doctype or head because
the Artifact platform supplies them. On GitHub Pages that rendered in quirks
mode and broke the full-height layout. The build now emits a standalone page
with the same skeleton the platform injects.

Also adds an on-map key, open by default, that explains the symbols -
especially the dashed red circles, which are the 20 state closed areas from
Fis 306.01 drawn at approximately the size of each closure.

Imagery now goes to zoom 19, and over satellite the water and marsh draw as
outlines so the real marsh edge stays readable.

